From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:20:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: name the SIO's
 registers

The T8132 sleep gate finds the CPU of each coprocessor that must stop
before the commit by its "coproc" or "asc" register name. The SIO node
has no reg-names, so on the J604, which enables the SIO for DisplayPort
audio, the gate cannot read whether its CPU stopped and refuses every
deep sleep: "dma-controller didn't stop: control 0x0 status 0x0".

Give the J604's SIO the names its binding defines. The SIO driver maps
its registers by index and is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 389d013872..070189b594 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -452,6 +452,16 @@ opp-4464000000 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The sleep gate finds a coprocessor's CPU by reg-names ("asc"); without
+ * them the SIO, which this board enables for DisplayPort audio, cannot be
+ * checked as stopped and every deep sleep is refused before its commit.
+ * The names are the binding's; apple-sio maps its registers by index.
+ */
+&sio {
+	reg-names = "asc", "auxiliary";
+};
+
 /* Deep sleep: the T8132 sleep controller, as the J713 enables it upstream. */
 &sleep {
 	/*
